<title>HONG KONG: Moody's says may cut ratings for five Thai banks.</title>
<headline>Moody's says may cut ratings for five Thai banks.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-02-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Moody's Investors Service said on Friday it may cut the A2 long-term foreign-currency bond and deposit ratings for five Thai banks.</p>
<p>The banks are Bangkok Bank, the Export-Import Bank of Thailand, Industrial Finance Corp of Thailand, Siam Commercial Bank and Thai Farmers' Bank.</p>
